SCRIPT='A contrarian mindset essay: hook (average student with a Tesla), Swedish ability-plateau study, five reasons - stupid grit (persistence, consistent investing), action over analysis (lawn-care friend), emotional intelligence, no fear of looking stupid (Pet Rock, cat drawings), and avoiding prestige spending (Ivy vs state school, plumber vs engineers) - and a habits close. Verified: the Swedish study design and top-1% finding (ESR 2023). Overstated/unsupported: top earners "a little bit dumber" (they are above average, only slightly below the next stratum); EQ "85-90% of success" (popular misquote); Ivy sticker-price comparison ignores aid; plumber/engineer anecdote unrepresentative. Few numeric claims; the cat-drawing revenue needs merchandise to reach $300K. The stored ending is complete.'
